# THE SIFREI ROWS on Deuteronomy 1:1-8 (THE DEUTERONOMY WALK sitting 1 — THE OPENING SPEECH, 2026-09-15): piskaot 1-8 by POSITION — the
# export's first eight, on 1:1 (1, twenty rows), 1:2 (2), 1:4 (3), 1:5 (4), 1:6 (5), 1:7 (6), 1:8 (7 and 8); forty-eight rows at the two
# files' equal grain, each opened and verdicted in BOTH files; the middah named where the row argues by one (logic/MIDDOT.md). The English's
# apparatus (page notes, footnotes) read past, not as rows. The shelf's Hebrew cut by consonants (deu_ink.SP_). Speed ruling (c): CONTEXT terse.
from deu_ink import *
S = {}
def srow(p, r, verdict, prose): S[(p, r)] = (verdict, prose)

srow(1, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"THESE ARE THE WORDS MOSES SPOKE" — DID MOSES PROPHESY ONLY THESE? HE WROTE THE WHOLE TORAH (31:9)! IT TEACHES THAT THESE WERE WORDS OF REBUKE, AS "JESHURUN GREW FAT AND KICKED" (32:15). The head row on 1:1 ({SP_(1, 1, "מלמד", "שהיו", "דברי", "תוכחות")} "it teaches that they were words of rebuke"): the book\'s first word read as a genre — the opening speech is a rebuke, the places its charges; the translation writes the same reading into the verse (Onkelos 1:1 \'he rebuked them\'). The middah: the redundancy resolved (I5) — \'these are the words\' against the whole written Torah.')
srow(1, 2, 'CONTEXT', 'THE SAME OF AMOS: "THE WORDS OF AMOS" (Amos 1:1) — DID HE PROPHESY ONLY THOSE? THEY WERE WORDS OF REBUKE ("HEAR THIS, COWS OF BASHAN" — THEIR COURTS). The parallel row: the genre proved on a second book (I5 again); the cows of Bashan read as the courts.')
srow(1, 3, 'CONTEXT', 'THE SAME OF JEREMIAH: "THESE ARE THE WORDS THE LORD SPOKE TO ISRAEL AND JUDAH" (Jeremiah 30:4) — HE WROTE TWO SCROLLS; WORDS OF REBUKE ("A VOICE OF TREMBLING"). The parallel row (I5).')
srow(1, 4, 'CONTEXT', 'THE SAME OF DAVID: "THESE ARE THE LAST WORDS OF DAVID" (2 Samuel 23:1) — "THE SPIRIT OF THE LORD SPOKE IN ME"; WORDS OF REBUKE ("THE WICKED ARE AS THORNS"). The parallel row (I5).')
srow(1, 5, 'CONTEXT', 'THE SAME OF SOLOMON: "THE WORDS OF KOHELETH" (Ecclesiastes 1:1) — HE WROTE THREE SCROLLS; WORDS OF REBUKE — THE SUN, THE WIND AND THE RIVERS THE WICKED WITHOUT REWARD. The parallel row (I5); the Hebrew reads 1:5-7 as the wicked likened to sun, moon and sea.')
srow(1, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"TO ALL ISRAEL" — HAD HE REBUKED ONLY SOME, THOSE IN THE MARKET WOULD SAY: YOU HEARD THIS FROM THE SON OF AMRAM AND ANSWERED NOTHING? HAD WE BEEN THERE WE WOULD HAVE ANSWERED FOUR OR FIVE TIMES! The row on 1:1\'s \'all\' ({SP_(1, 6, "אלו", "הוכיח", "מקצתם")} "had he rebuked some of them"): the whole assembly so that no absent man could boast. The middah: the inclusion read from \'all\' (I2).')
srow(1, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "TO ALL ISRAEL" — MOSES GATHERED THEM FROM THE GREATEST TO THE SMALLEST AND SAID: I AM REBUKING YOU; WHOEVER HAS AN ANSWER, LET HIM COME AND SAY IT. ({SP_(1, 7, "כל", "מי", "שיש", "לו", "תשובה", "יבוא", "ויאמר")} "whoever has an answer let him come and say") — the rebuke offered to reply. (I2.)')
srow(1, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "TO ALL ISRAEL" — ALL WERE MASTERS OF REBUKE AND ABLE TO BEAR IT. R. TARFON: BY THE SERVICE, IS THERE ONE IN THIS GENERATION WHO CAN REBUKE! R. ELAZAR BEN AZARIAH: WHO CAN RECEIVE REBUKE! R. AKIVA: WHO KNOWS HOW! R. YOHANAN BEN NURI: MORE THAN FIVE TIMES AKIVA WAS CHASTISED ON MY ACCOUNT BEFORE RABBAN GAMLIEL AT YAVNEH, AND HE LOVED ME THE MORE — "REBUKE A WISE MAN AND HE WILL LOVE YOU" (Proverbs 9:8). The generation\'s row ({SP_(1, 8, "אם", "יש", "בדור", "הזה", "מי", "שיכול", "להוכיח")} "if there is in this generation one who can rebuke"); the English reads the first clause as a question. Prior read: gen_29\'s ledger names 8:1 (piska 8), not this row.')
srow(1, 9, 'MATERIAL', f'"BEYOND THE JORDAN" — HE REBUKED THEM FOR WHAT THEY DID BEYOND THE JORDAN. The first place read as a charge ({SP_(1, 9, "מלמד", "שהוכיחם", "על", "מה", "שעשו", "בעבר", "הירדן")} "it teaches that he rebuked them for what they did beyond the Jordan") — the English\'s note: Shittim (Numbers 25). The middah: the place-name read as an allusion (E32\'s kin, the aggadic name-reading) — the row\'s form repeated for every name of 1:1.')
srow(1, 10, 'MATERIAL', f'"IN THE WILDERNESS" — FOR WHAT THEY DID IN THE WILDERNESS. ANOTHER WORD: THEY THREW THEIR LITTLE SONS AND DAUGHTERS INTO MOSES\' LAP: SON OF AMRAM, WHAT PROVISION HAVE YOU PREPARED FOR THESE? R. JUDAH: "WOULD WE HAD DIED BY THE HAND OF THE LORD IN EGYPT" (Exodus 16:3). The wilderness charge ({SP_(1, 10, "בן", "עמרם", "מה", "אנונה", "התקנת", "להם", "לאלו")} "son of Amram, what provision have you prepared for these") — the manna\'s complaint (Exodus 16:3 cited).')
srow(1, 11, 'CONTEXT', 'ANOTHER WORD: "IN THE WILDERNESS" — THE GENERAL RULE FOR ALL THEY DID IN THE WILDERNESS. The wilderness as the whole.')
srow(1, 12, 'MATERIAL', f'"IN THE ARABAH" — FOR WHAT THEY DID IN THE PLAINS OF MOAB: "AND ISRAEL DWELT IN SHITTIM" (Numbers 25:1). ({SP_(1, 12, "על", "מה", "שעשו", "בערבות", "מואב")} "for what they did in the plains of Moab") — the Arabah read as the plains of Moab, Peor the charge (the Sifrei 30:1 closes the sitting\'s span on Peor).')
srow(1, 13, 'MATERIAL', f'"OPPOSITE SUPH" — FOR WHAT THEY DID AT THE SEA: THEY REBELLED AT THE SEA AND TURNED THEIR BACK ON MOSES THREE JOURNEYS; R. JUDAH: AT THE SEA AND IN THE SEA — "THEY REBELLED AT THE SEA, IN THE SEA OF REEDS" (Psalm 106:7). BETWEEN JOURNEY AND JOURNEY? "BETWEEN PARAN AND TOPHEL AND LABAN" — WORDS OF FOLLY THEY SPOKE AGAINST THE MANNA ("OUR SOUL LOATHES THE LIGHT BREAD", Numbers 21:5): FOOLS, KINGS CHOOSE LIGHT BREAD; YOU WENT IN THE FOLLY OF YOUR FATHER ADAM — "THE WOMAN YOU GAVE ME" (Genesis 3:12). The row that carries THE COMPLAINT TEMPLATE ({SP_(1, 13, "דברי", "תפלות", "שתפלו", "על", "המן")} "words of folly they spoke against the manna" — Tophel read by its consonants, the translation\'s \'where they scorned the manna\'): read before by topic in gen_09 and gen_10 (Adam\'s answer as the template of complaint) — named, not fresh. The middot: the name read by its sound (the aggadic move that splits a name into words) and the a-fortiori of the good repaid with complaint.')
srow(1, 14, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND HAZEROTH" — SHOULD YOU NOT HAVE LEARNED FROM WHAT I DID TO MIRIAM AT HAZEROTH? IF I DID NOT FAVOR RIGHTEOUS MIRIAM IN JUDGMENT, HOW MUCH MORE OTHER MEN. ({SP_(1, 14, "לא", "היה", "לכם", "ללמד", "ממה", "שעשיתי", "למרים")} "should you not have learned from what I did to Miriam") — Numbers 12 the charge; the middah: a fortiori (I1) from the righteous to the rest.')
srow(1, 15, 'CONTEXT', 'ANOTHER WORD: IF MIRIAM, WHO SPOKE ONLY AGAINST HER YOUNGER BROTHER, WAS SO PUNISHED, ONE WHO SPEAKS AGAINST HIS SUPERIOR HOW MUCH MORE. (I1.)')
srow(1, 16, 'CONTEXT', 'ANOTHER WORD: IF MIRIAM, WHOM NO CREATURE HEARD BUT THE OMNIPRESENT ("AND THE LORD HEARD", Numbers 12:2), WAS SO PUNISHED, ONE WHO SHAMES HIS FELLOW IN PUBLIC HOW MUCH MORE. (I1.)')
srow(1, 17, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND DI-ZAHAB" — HE SAID: THIS OUTWEIGHS ALL; OF ALL YOU DID, THE CALF IS HARDEST FOR ME. R. JUDAH\'S PARABLE: THE LAST TROUBLE ADDED TO MANY. R. SHIMON\'S: THE HOST WHO RECEIVED SAGES, THEN GENTILES, THEN ROBBERS — "GOLD ENOUGH FOR THE TABERNACLE, GOLD ENOUGH FOR THE CALF". R. BENAIAH: LET THE TABERNACLE\'S GOLD ATONE FOR THE CALF\'S. R. YOSE BEN HANINA: "A MERCY SEAT OF PURE GOLD" (Exodus 25:17) — LET THE COVER\'S GOLD ATONE FOR THE CALF\'S. ({SP_(1, 17, "מעשה", "עגל", "קשה", "עלי", "מן", "הכל")} "the deed of the calf is hardest for me") — Di-zahab read as the gold of the calf, the translation\'s \'the calf of gold\'; the atonement by the same metal.')
srow(1, 18, 'MATERIAL', f'R. JUDAH: "IN THE WILDERNESS, IN THE ARABAH..." — THESE ARE THE TEN TRIALS OUR FATHERS TRIED THE OMNIPRESENT: TWO AT THE SEA, TWO AT THE WATERS, TWO AT THE MANNA, TWO AT THE QUAIL, ONE AT THE CALF, ONE AT PARAN WITH THE SPIES. R. YOSE BEN DORMASKIT: JUDAH, WHY DO YOU TWIST THE SCRIPTURES ON US? I CALL HEAVEN AND EARTH TO WITNESS, WE HAVE GONE OVER ALL THE PLACES AND THEY ARE PLACES, NAMED FOR AN EVENT — "HE CALLED THE WELL ESEK... SHIBAH" (Genesis 26:20-33). THE DISPUTE ROW ({SP_(1, 18, "ואינם", "מקומות", "שנקראו", "אלא", "על", "שם", "מאורע")} "and they are places called after an event"): the ten trials against the plain places — the two readings of 1:1 the Sifrei itself holds open (the compile\'s docket: which reading the code carries).')
srow(1, 19, 'CONTEXT', 'THE SAME DISPUTE ON ZECHARIAH 9:1 "HADRACH" — R. JUDAH: THE MESSIAH, HARSH TO THE NATIONS AND SOFT TO ISRAEL; R. YOSE: I AM FROM DAMASCUS AND THERE IS A PLACE NAMED HADRACH; "DAMASCUS HIS RESTING PLACE" — JERUSALEM WILL REACH TO DAMASCUS; THE LAND WIDENS LIKE A FIG (Ezekiel 41:7); THE EXILES CAMP IN IT (Isaiah 2:2-3). The parallel dispute (outside the verse).')
srow(1, 20, 'CONTEXT', 'THE SAME ON GENESIS 41:43 "AVRECH" — R. JUDAH: A FATHER IN WISDOM, TENDER IN YEARS; R. YOSE: "I WILL MAKE THEM KNEEL" — ALL WENT IN AND OUT UNDER HIS HAND. The parallel dispute (outside the verse).')
srow(2, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"ELEVEN DAYS FROM HOREB BY WAY OF MOUNT SEIR TO KADESH-BARNEA" — IS IT ELEVEN DAYS FROM HOREB TO KIBROTH-HATTAAVAH, TO HAZEROTH, TO PARAN? IS IT NOT THREE DAYS\' JOURNEY (Numbers 10:33)? R. JUDAH: DID ISRAEL WALK ELEVEN STATIONS IN THREE DAYS? IS IT NOT FORTY DAYS\' JOURNEY, AS ELIJAH\'S (1 Kings 19:8)? SINCE YOU SAY IT IS IMPOSSIBLE, RETURN TO THE FIRST MATTER. The head row on 1:2 ({SP_(2, 1, "והלא", "אינו", "אלא", "מהלך", "שלשה", "ימים")} "is it not only a journey of three days"): the eleven days against Numbers 10:33\'s three and Elijah\'s forty — the ink\'s [11] measured against the stations (the compile\'s question).')
srow(2, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"ELEVEN DAYS" — HAD ISRAEL MERITED, IN ELEVEN DAYS THEY WOULD HAVE ENTERED; SINCE THEY CORRUPTED THEIR DEEDS THE OMNIPRESENT TURNED FORTY DAYS INTO FORTY YEARS (Numbers 14:34). R. JUDAH: IN THREE DAYS — "THE ARK... THREE DAYS\' JOURNEY TO SEEK THEM A RESTING PLACE" (Numbers 10:33), THE RESTING PLACE THE LAND (12:9). R. BENAIAH: IN ONE DAY — "TODAY YOU GO OUT... AND WHEN THE LORD BRINGS YOU" (Exodus 13:4-5), AT ONCE. ABBA YOSE BEN HANAN: AS SOON AS THEIR FEET LEFT THE SEA — "GO UP, POSSESS" (1:21), AT ONCE. ({SP_(2, 2, "אלו", "זכו", "ישראל", "לאחד", "עשר", "יום", "היו")} "had Israel merited, in eleven days they would have") — FOUR MEASURES OF THE DELAY: eleven days, three, one, none; 1:21\'s \'go up, possess\' read \'at once\' (the Sifrei 19:3 reads it so again). The middah: the number as the measure of merit.')
srow(2, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"IN THE FORTIETH YEAR, IN THE ELEVENTH MONTH" — IT TEACHES THAT THE YEAR HAS TWELVE MONTHS. DO WE NOT KNOW IT? "THE TWELFTH MONTH, ADAR" (Esther 3:13); SOLOMON\'S TWELVE OFFICERS AND "ONE OFFICER IN THE LAND" (1 Kings 4:7, 19) — THE INTERCALATED MONTH. R. BENAIAH: BEFORE SOLOMON DID WE NOT KNOW? "A HUNDRED AND TWENTY YEARS OLD AM I TODAY" (31:2) — TODAY MY DAYS ARE FULL; "THE PEOPLE CAME UP FROM THE JORDAN ON THE TENTH OF THE FIRST MONTH" (Joshua 4:19) — COUNT BACK THIRTY-THREE DAYS AND THE YEAR IS TWELVE MONTHS. ({SP_(2, 3, "מלמד", "שהשנה", "שנים", "עשר", "חדש")} "it teaches that the year is twelve months") — the date read for the calendar: the eleventh month, the first of the month, Moses\' death on the seventh of the twelfth, thirty-three days to the crossing. THE COMPILE\'S CLOCK: the parser\'s [40, 11, 1] joins Numbers 33:38\'s [40, 5] — Aaron\'s death in the fifth month, Moses\' speech in the eleventh, six months apart on one clock.')
srow(2, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "IN THE FORTIETH YEAR" — HE REBUKED THEM ONLY NEAR DEATH. FROM WHOM? FROM JACOB (Genesis 49:1-3: "REUBEN MY FIRSTBORN" — I DID NOT REBUKE YOU ALL THESE YEARS LEST YOU LEAVE ME AND CLEAVE TO ESAU). FOUR REASONS ONE REBUKES ONLY NEAR DEATH: NOT TO REBUKE AND REBUKE AGAIN; THAT HIS FELLOW NOT SEE HIM AND BE ASHAMED; THAT HE BEAR NO GRUDGE; THAT THEY PART IN PEACE — REBUKE BRINGS PEACE. ({SP_(2, 4, "מלמד", "שלא", "הוכיחם", "אלא", "סמוך", "למיתה")} "it teaches that he rebuked them only near death") — the date read as the timing of rebuke; the outside row 54:2 carries the same from 1:4 (\'after he had smitten Sihon\').')
srow(2, 5, 'CONTEXT', 'SO ABRAHAM: "ABRAHAM REBUKED ABIMELECH" (Genesis 21:25) — AND "THE TWO CUT A COVENANT" (21:27); SO ISAAC: "WHY HAVE YOU COME TO ME?" (26:27) — AND "THEY WENT FROM HIM IN PEACE" (26:31). Rebuke ending in peace — the four reasons\' proofs.')
srow(2, 6, 'CONTEXT', 'SO JOSHUA REBUKED ISRAEL ONLY NEAR DEATH ("CHOOSE THIS DAY", Joshua 24:15; "WITNESSES", 24:21); SO SAMUEL ("TESTIFY AGAINST ME", 1 Samuel 12:3-5). The near-death rebukes.')
srow(2, 7, 'CONTEXT', 'SO DAVID REBUKED SOLOMON HIS SON ONLY NEAR DEATH ("THE DAYS OF DAVID DREW NEAR TO DIE AND HE CHARGED SOLOMON", 1 Kings 2:1). The near-death rebukes.')
srow(2, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'"MOSES SPOKE TO ALL ISRAEL" — DID MOSES PROPHESY ONLY "THESE ARE THE WORDS"? WHENCE ALL THE UTTERANCES OF THE TORAH, THE LIGHT AND THE WEIGHTY, THE EQUAL DECREES, THE GENERAL AND THE PARTICULAR, THE BODIES AND THE DETAILS? "MOSES SPOKE ACCORDING TO ALL THAT THE LORD COMMANDED HIM" (1:3). THE RECEIPT READ FOR THE RULES ({SP_(2, 8, "הקלות", "והחמורות", "הגזרות", "שוות", "הכללות", "והפרטות")} "the light and the weighty, the equal decrees, the generals and the particulars"): \'according to ALL\' — the hermeneutic rules themselves (the a-fortiori, the gezerah shavah, the general-and-particular) inside the receipt form; the register\'s seat at 1:3 filed NONE meets its reading here — THE COMPILE\'S DOCKET: the receipt that receives the rules (I1, I2, I4 named by the row itself).')
srow(3, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AFTER HE HAD SMITTEN SIHON" — A PARABLE OF A KING WHO WENT OUT WITH HIS ARMIES TO THE WILDERNESS; THEY ASKED HOT LOAVES; HE SAID: I GIVE; THEY ASKED AGAIN; HIS OFFICER SAID: BECAUSE THE KING IS FIT, WHENCE MILLS AND OVENS IN THE WILDERNESS? The head row on 1:4 ({SP_(3, 1, "משל", "למלך", "שיצא", "הוא", "וחילותיו", "למדבר")} "a parable of a king who went out, he and his armies, to the wilderness") — the English notes the text is thought flawed; the parable\'s point in 3:2.')
srow(3, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'SO MOSES SAID: IF I REBUKE ISRAEL FIRST, THEY WILL SAY: BECAUSE HE HAS NO STRENGTH TO BRING US IN AND FELL SIHON AND OG, HE REBUKES US. HE DID NOT; ONLY AFTER HE BROUGHT THEM IN AND FELLED SIHON AND OG DID HE REBUKE THEM — "AFTER HE HAD SMITTEN SIHON". ({SP_(3, 2, "אלא", "לאחר", "שהכניסם", "לארץ", "והפיל", "סיחון", "ועוג")} "only after he brought them into the land and felled Sihon and Og") — 1:4\'s \'after\' read as the timing that forecloses the taunt (the outside row 54:2 the same).')
srow(3, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHO DWELT IN HESHBON" — HAD SIHON NOT BEEN HARD BUT DWELT IN HESHBON, HE WAS HARD, FOR THE PROVINCE WAS HARD; HAD THE PROVINCE NOT BEEN HARD BUT SIHON IN IT, IT WAS HARD, FOR THE KING WAS HARD; HOW MUCH MORE WHEN KING AND PROVINCE ARE HARD! ({SP_(3, 3, "על", "אחת", "כמה", "וכמה", "שהמלך", "קשה", "והמדינה")} "how much more when the king is hard and the province") — the a-fortiori (I1) on the two.')
srow(3, 4, 'CONTEXT', 'THE SAME OF OG IN ASHTAROTH — HAD OG NOT BEEN HARD... HOW MUCH MORE. (I1.)')
srow(3, 5, 'CONTEXT', '"IN ASHTAROTH" — HARD AS ASHTAROTH; "IN EDREI" — THE SEAT OF THE KINGDOM. The names read.')
srow(4, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"BEYOND THE JORDAN IN THE LAND OF MOAB MOSES TOOK UPON HIMSELF TO EXPLAIN" — R. JUDAH: "TOOK UPON HIMSELF" MEANS A BEGINNING ("BE PLEASED TO STAY THE NIGHT", Judges 19:6; "YOU HAVE BEGUN TO BLESS", 1 Chronicles 17:27); THE SAGES: AN OATH ("MOSES SWORE TO DWELL WITH THE MAN", Exodus 2:21; "SAUL ADJURED THE PEOPLE", 1 Samuel 14:24). The head row on 1:5 ({SP_(4, 1, "אין", "הואלה", "אלא", "התחלה")} "\'undertaking\' is nothing but a beginning"; {SP_(4, 1, "אין", "הואלה", "אלא", "שבועה")} "\'undertaking\' is nothing but an oath"): the store\'s \'yield\' glossed by the verb\'s own dispute; the translation takes R. Judah\'s (\'Moses began\'); the Sifrei 27:1 takes the sages\' (Moses\' oath to Jethro). The middah: the word\'s sense fixed from its other seats (E7, the narrative verbal analogy — the word fixed from its other seats).')
srow(4, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"TO EXPLAIN THIS TORAH, SAYING" — HE SAID: I AM NEAR DEATH; WHOEVER HEARD ONE VERSE AND FORGOT IT, LET HIM COME AND REPEAT IT; ONE SECTION, ONE CHAPTER, ONE LAW — LET HIM COME AND REPEAT IT. ({SP_(4, 2, "מי", "ששמע", "פסוק", "אחד", "ושכחו", "יבוא", "וישננו")} "whoever heard one verse and forgot it, let him come and repeat it") — \'explain\' read as review before death, in four grains: verse, section, chapter, law.')
srow(5, 1, 'CONTEXT', '"THE LORD OUR GOD SPOKE TO US AT HOREB, SAYING" — MOSES: NOT FROM MYSELF DO I SPEAK TO YOU BUT FROM THE MOUTH OF THE HOLY ONE. The refrain (9:1, 19:1, 25:6 the same).')
srow(5, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOU HAVE DWELT LONG ENOUGH AT THIS MOUNTAIN" — IT WAS REWARD FOR YOU, YOUR DWELLING AT THIS MOUNTAIN: YOU MADE THE TABERNACLE, THE TABLE, THE LAMPSTAND. ANOTHER WORD: IT WAS BENEFIT FOR YOU: YOU RECEIVED THE TORAH, APPOINTED SEVENTY ELDERS, APPOINTED CAPTAINS OF THOUSANDS, HUNDREDS, FIFTIES AND TENS — A GREAT BENEFIT. ({SP_(5, 2, "שכר", "הוא", "לכם", "ישיבתכם", "בהר", "הזה")} "it is reward for you, your dwelling at this mountain") — \'enough\' (רב, "much") read as much good: the tabernacle, the Torah, the elders, the officers of 1:15 named at Horeb. The middah: the homonym read (\'much\' for \'enough\').')
srow(5, 3, 'CONTEXT', 'ANOTHER WORD: IT IS HARM FOR YOU, YOUR DWELLING AT THIS MOUNTAIN. The third reading.')
srow(5, 4, 'CONTEXT', '"TURN AND JOURNEY" (1:7) — IDLENESS IS HARM. The move ordered against idleness.')
srow(6, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"TURN AND JOURNEY, GO" — BY WAY OF ARAD AND HORMAH. "THE HILL COUNTRY OF THE AMORITES AND ALL ITS NEIGHBORS" — AMMON, MOAB AND MOUNT SEIR. "IN THE ARABAH" — THE PLAIN OF ZOAR. "THE HILL" — THE KING\'S HILL. "THE LOWLAND" — THE LOWLAND OF LOD AND OF THE SOUTH. "THE NEGEB AND THE COAST" — GAZA, ASHKELON AND CAESAREA. "THE LAND OF THE CANAANITE" — ITS BORDER (Genesis 10:19). THE GEOGRAPHY ROW ({SP_(6, 1, "זה", "מישור", "של", "צוער")} "this is the plain of Zoar"; {SP_(6, 1, "זה", "הר", "המלך")} "this is the King\'s Hill"): 1:7\'s regions as Mishnah Sheviit 9:2\'s three lands and their divisions — read before by topic in gen_24 (material there for the nations\' border) — named, not fresh; the compile\'s map.')
srow(6, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND LEBANON" — WHEN YOU ENTER THE LAND YOU MUST SET UP A KING AND BUILD THE CHOSEN HOUSE. LEBANON IS A KING ("HE CAME TO LEBANON AND TOOK THE TOP OF THE CEDAR", Ezekiel 17:3; "THE THISTLE IN LEBANON", 2 Kings 14:9) AND LEBANON IS THE TEMPLE ("GILEAD YOU ARE TO ME, THE HEAD OF LEBANON", Jeremiah 22:6; "LEBANON SHALL FALL BY A MIGHTY ONE", Isaiah 10:34). ({SP_(6, 2, "ואין", "לבנון", "אלא", "בית", "המקדש")} "and Lebanon is nothing but the Temple") — the translation writes it at 3:25 (\'the house of the sanctuary\'), not here (Onkelos 1:7 keeps Lebanon). The middah: E7 — the word fixed from its other seats.')
srow(6, 3, 'CONTEXT', 'ANOTHER WORD: WHY LEBANON? IT WHITENS ISRAEL\'S SINS — "THOUGH YOUR SINS BE AS SCARLET, THEY SHALL BE WHITE AS SNOW" (Isaiah 1:18). The name by its sound (28:3 repeats it).')
srow(6, 4, 'CONTEXT', '"TO THE GREAT RIVER, THE RIVER EUPHRATES" — ITS BULK AND STRENGTH FACE THE LAND OF ISRAEL; THE ADAGE: THE KING\'S SERVANT IS A KING; CLEAVE TO A BOIL AND IT BURNS YOU. Genesis 15:18\'s river at its second seat (the ink).')
srow(6, 5, 'CONTEXT', 'ANOTHER WORD: IT DIVIDES AND GOES UNTIL IT ENDS IN THE SHOVEL; ANOTHER: FRUITFUL AND GREAT UNTIL THEY CROSS IT IN SHIPS; THE RIVERS ASK WHY ITS VOICE IS NOT HEARD — MY DEEDS TESTIFY: SEED IN ME RISES IN THREE DAYS, A PLANT IN THIRTY; SCRIPTURE PRAISES ME. The name read by its sound (Perath: divides, fruitful).')
srow(7, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"SEE, I HAVE SET THE LAND BEFORE YOU" — I TELL YOU NOT BY ESTIMATE NOR BY HEARSAY BUT WHAT YOU SEE WITH YOUR EYES. "GO IN AND POSSESS" — WHEN YOU ENTER YOU NEED NO WEAPONS, ONLY A SURVEYOR TO DIVIDE. ({SP_(7, 1, "לא", "מאמד", "ולא", "משמועה", "אלא", "מה", "שאתם")} "not by estimate nor by hearsay but what you"; {SP_(7, 1, "אלא", "קובע", "דיופטין", "ומחלק")} "only setting a surveyor and dividing") — \'see\' read as the witness\'s charge (Sanhedrin 4:5; 19:3 repeats it); \'possess\' as division without war — the compile\'s witness rule.')
srow(8, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHICH THE LORD SWORE TO YOUR FATHERS" — WHY "TO ABRAHAM, TO ISAAC AND TO JACOB"? IF FOR THE OATHS, "THE OATHS TO THE TRIBES" IS SAID (Habakkuk 3:9). ABRAHAM WORTHY ALONE, ISAAC ALONE, JACOB ALONE. A PARABLE: THE KING GAVE HIS SERVANT A FIELD AS IT WAS; THE SERVANT IMPROVED IT, PLANTED A VINEYARD — "WHAT IS IN MY HAND? HE GAVE IT AS IT WAS". SO THE LAND GIVEN TO ABRAHAM AS IT WAS ("WALK THE LAND", Genesis 13:17); ABRAHAM IMPROVED IT (THE TAMARISK, 21:33), ISAAC (THE HUNDREDFOLD, 26:12), JACOB (THE FIELD BOUGHT, 33:19). THE GIVEN-AS-IS ROW ({SP_(8, 1, "לא", "נתנה", "לו", "אלא", "כמות", "שהיא")} "he gave it to him only as it is") — read before by topic in gen_29 (material there: the Land given as-is, the patriarchs\' improvements) — named, not fresh. The middah: the redundant triad resolved to three merits (I5).')
srow(8, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"TO GIVE TO THEM" — THOSE WHO ENTERED THE LAND; "AND TO THEIR SEED" — THEIR SONS; "AFTER THEM" — WHAT DAVID AND JEROBOAM CONQUERED ("HE RESTORED THE BORDER OF ISRAEL FROM THE ENTRANCE OF HAMATH", 2 Kings 14:25). ({SP_(8, 2, "אלו", "שכבשו", "דוד", "וירבעם")} "these are what David and Jeroboam conquered") — 1:8\'s three datives as three generations of possession; Jeroboam son of Joash\'s border the third.')
srow(8, 3, 'CONTEXT', 'RABBI: "TO THEM" — THOSE WHO CAME UP FROM BABYLON; "THEIR SEED" — THEIR SONS; "AFTER THEM" — THE DAYS OF THE MESSIAH. The second reading of the three.')
assert sorted(S) == [(p, r) for p in range(1, 9) for r in range(1, SIF_ROWS[p] + 1)], sorted(S)
